---
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { pick } from '../data/faq';
---
<Guide
  page="homelab"
  lede="Your media apps run on a server, and Cupola reaches it too: TrueNAS, Unraid, Dockge and Nginx Proxy Manager, in the same app."
  services={['truenas', 'unraid', 'dockge', 'nginx_proxy_manager']}
  questions={pick('away', 'certs', 'tested')}
  related={['downloads', 'stream', 'contribute']}
>
  <h2>The whole lab on one screen</h2>
  <p>The Stack tab shows every service and which ones need a look. A stopped container or a failing disk lands in <em>Needs you</em>, next to stuck downloads, with the fix.</p>

  <h2>TrueNAS</h2>
  <p>A full console: pools, disks, datasets, snapshots, shares, apps, virtual machines, replication, tasks, reports and users. A disk with errors offers the scrub that repairs it.</p>

  <h2>Unraid</h2>
  <p>Array, disks, shares, Docker containers, VMs and notifications. Start and stop VMs. Tested against recorded answers only so far: if you run Unraid, tell us how it goes.</p>

  <h2>Dockge</h2>
  <p>Your compose stacks with live terminal output. Start, stop, restart and update them, or edit and deploy the compose file.</p>

  <h2>Nginx Proxy Manager</h2>
  <p>Your hosts, what is broken, and which certificates expire soon. Turn hosts on or off and renew certificates. It signs in with email and password, the only login it offers.</p>
</Guide>
